     "body": "<p>I added a \"how-to\" page that goes into depth about the feature and linked to it from the place in that configuration options inventory.</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://wiki.duraspace.org/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=85529498\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://wiki.duraspace.org/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=85529498</a></p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://wiki.duraspace.org/pages/diffpagesbyversion.action?pageId=67242898&amp;selectedPageVersions=15&amp;selectedPageVersions=14\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://wiki.duraspace.org/pages/diffpagesbyversion.action?pageId=67242898&amp;selectedPageVersions=15&amp;selectedPageVersions=14</a></p>\n\n<p>I think this will meet the following two likely use cases:</p>\n<ol>\n\t<li>someone who \"reads the manual\" and goes through the configuration options methodically looking for what they want or simply familiarizing themself with the options</li>\n\t<li>someone who knows what they want to do, thinks it's possible and searches google or the wiki for how to do it.  (should soon be able to find the \"how to\" page when searching for something like \"fcrepo modify createdBy\" or \"fcrepo modify server managed triples\") (<a href=\"https://wiki.duraspace.org/dosearchsite.action?queryString=modify+server+managed+triples\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">search in confluence</a>)</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<p> </p>",
